  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "She cut the labels out of every piece of clothing. Every prescription, every maker's mark, scraped off or burned away.",
        "visual_query": "norwegian mountain valley autumn bergen",
        "visual_fallback": "mountain valley"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Hikers found her on the twenty-ninth of November, 1970, in Isdalen valley outside Bergen. Her face was gone, her clothes scorched.",
        "visual_query": "cold rocky ravine norway hiking",
        "visual_fallback": "rocky ravine"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Police traced two suitcases to Bergen railway station. Wigs, foreign currency, a coded notebook, a prescription bottle with no name.",
        "visual_query": "old railway station luggage locker",
        "visual_fallback": "station lockers"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Decoded, the notebook was an itinerary. She had crossed Europe under at least eight passports, calling herself Belgian, writing in German or French.",
        "visual_query": "vintage european passports travel documents",
        "visual_fallback": "old passports"
      },
      {
        "narration": "In 2017, isotopes in her teeth put her childhood near Nuremberg, born around 1930. Nobody has matched that to a name.",
        "visual_query": "nuremberg german old town street",
        "visual_fallback": "german town"
      }
    ],
